<figure class="visual">
        <figcaption class="visual-cap"><span class="label">Bird’s-eye architecture</span><h3>Global traffic delivery and regional inspection</h3><p>Read top to bottom for ingress. The inspected egress lane is a separate route-controlled path inside the Mumbai example.</p></figcaption>
        <div class="architecture" role="img" aria-label="Internet clients enter AWS Global Accelerator. Separate listeners reach ALB and NLB endpoints in Mumbai and Hyderabad. In Mumbai, a separate egress route sends workload traffic through a Gateway Load Balancer endpoint and appliance fleet before NAT and internet egress.">
          <div class="arch-entry"><div class="node"><b>Clients and internet users</b><small>global traffic entry</small></div><div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="arch-ga"><strong>AWS Global Accelerator · global edge</strong><p>Static anycast addresses · AWS global network · health-based regional endpoint selection</p><p><span class="mono">TCP :443 → ALB endpoints</span> · <span class="mono">TCP :8443 → NLB endpoints</span></p></div></div>
          <div class="arch-regions">
            <section class="arch-region" aria-labelledby="mumbai-overview"><header><div><strong id="mumbai-overview">Region 1 · Mumbai</strong><span>ap-south-1</span></div><span>endpoint groups per listener</span></header><div class="arch-services"><div class="arch-service alb"><b>ALB · application · L7</b><span>HTTP/HTTPS · content rules · TLS termination · AWS WAF</span></div><div class="arch-service nlb"><b>NLB · network · L4</b><span>Transport listeners · flow mapping · zonal static addresses</span></div></div><div class="arch-targets"><div class="arch-target">Private web/API targets<br/>EC2 · ECS · IP · Lambda where supported</div><div class="arch-target">Private service targets<br/>EC2 · ECS · IP · ALB where supported</div></div><div class="egress-lane"><strong>INSPECTED EGRESS · SEPARATE ROUTED PATH</strong><div class="egress-flow"><div>Private workload</div><div>GWLB endpoint</div><div>NAT gateway</div><div>Internet gateway</div></div><div class="appliance-branch"><span>GWLB endpoint</span><span>⇄ PrivateLink ⇄</span><span>GWLB ⇄ GENEVE :6081 ⇄ appliance fleet</span></div></div></section>
            <section class="arch-region" aria-labelledby="hyderabad-overview"><header><div><strong id="hyderabad-overview">Region 2 · Hyderabad</strong><span>ap-south-2</span></div><span>endpoint groups per listener</span></header><div class="arch-services"><div class="arch-service alb"><b>ALB · application · L7</b><span>HTTP/HTTPS · request rules · regional targets</span></div><div class="arch-service nlb"><b>NLB · network · L4</b><span>Transport listeners · flow targets · zonal addresses</span></div></div><div class="arch-targets"><div class="arch-target">Private web/API targets</div><div class="arch-target">Private network-service targets</div></div><div class="arch-notes"><div><b>1 · Global choice</b>Global Accelerator selects a healthy regional endpoint.</div><div><b>2 · Regional choice</b>ALB reads HTTP; NLB maps a transport flow.</div><div><b>3 · Routed inspection</b>GWLB distributes a separate routed flow to appliances.</div></div></section>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway"><strong>Three decisions:</strong> Global Accelerator selects regional entry; ALB or NLB selects an application target; GWLB scales an appliance hop on a route-controlled inspection path.</div>
        <div class="legend"><span>runtime traffic</span><span class="config">configuration or health</span><span class="tunnel">GENEVE tunnel</span><span class="broken">unavailable or dropped</span></div>
